/Ewall198","html_url":"https://github.com/Ewall198","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T19:22:14Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T19:22:14Z","body":"@mihe Tagging you to let you know that this PR exists. Not sure what the normal process is to get visibility/review here.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2752301587/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754397708","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103958#issuecomment-2754397708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103958","id":2754397708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kLMYM","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T13:26:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T13:26:23Z","body":"Since there is no active physics maintainer, I think this is a good idea.\r\n\r\nDo we need feature parity with godot physics?\r\n\r\nIs everyone ok with merging this?\r\n\r\nWhat would an alternative next best option?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754397708/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754889698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103958#issuecomment-2754889698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103958","id":2754889698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kNEfi","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T15:44:04Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T02:51:36Z","body":"> Not sure what the normal process is to get visibility/review here.\r\n\r\nAs mentioned already, Godot is somewhat underserved on the physics side of things, and while I'm happy to review the Jolt integration side of things when I can find the time (which has been scarce lately) the stuff that touches the shared `PhysicsServer3D` interface makes things a bit more complicated.\r\n\r\nI do think both Jolt's `JPH::DistanceConstraint` and `JPH::FixedConstraint` (as seen in #101575) make sense to add to the shared interface, since they seem to fill gaps in the various configurations of degrees-of-freedom that the existing joints can't really satisfy, and something like a `JoltDistanceConstraint3D` would set a new precedent that I'm not sure would be what we want.\r\n\r\nThey both seem mostly applicable to other physics engines as well, although I'm not seeing any equivalent to `JPH::DistanceConstraint` in Bullet, Rapier or ODE, but PhysX, Havok, BEPUphysics, Avian and Newton all seem to have it, which I guess should be enough, assuming that's an important consideration to begin with.\r\n\r\nHowever, with Jolt still being considered an experimental module, and with Godot Physics still being the default for some foreseeable future, I am a bit hesitant about adding stuff like this without a Godot Physics implementation. I suppose there is some highly theoretical future where this evaluation of Jolt as a replacement for Godot Physics results in not going forward with Jolt, and we're left with no-op scene nodes that do nothing but throw errors.\r\n\r\nAll that is to say that I don't really know what to do here. I would personally prefer to see that these kinds of Jolt-only PRs be put on hold until we at least make Jolt the default 3D physics engine, at which point adding this becomes a no-brainer, which could be as soon as Godot 4.5 I guess, but the criteria for that switch is not really well-defined, and making people wait until Godot 4.6 (or whenever) for this stuff to be available isn't ideal either.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs for the PR itself, from just a quick look...\r\n\r\nI would first of all ask that you rename this to be `DistanceJoint` and not `DistanceConstraint`, since that's how Godot (and some other physics engines) refer to these things.\r\n\r\nSecondly, as you already touched on yourself, the joint should probably expose springs in the form of stiffness and damping, as opposed to frequency and damping, to line up with the spring properties of the 6DOF joint. I realize frequency is arguably more useful and intuitive, and that 6DOF springs aren't implemented in Godot Physics anyway, but this will be changed for all springs to expose _both_ at some later point, when we Jolt-ify the joint interfaces in some way.\r\n\r\nBesides that it mostly looks very similar to the other joints (except for maybe the `are_bodies_switched` stuff, which looks a bit off) so is probably fine, but I'd need to do a deeper dive to say for sure, which I don't have time for right now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754889698/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777277284","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103958#issuecomment-2777277284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103958","id":2777277284,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lieNk","user":{"login":"Ewall198","id":8436683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MzY2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8436683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198","html_url":"https://github.com/Ewall198","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T00:33:01Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T00:34:09Z","body":"@mihe yeah the `are_bodies_switched` is to handle this automatic switching of bodies in `joint_3d::_update_joint` when `node_a`\r\nis `nullptr`. If the bodies get switched, we need to switch the relative anchor points too.\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/8bd9cdeea6d3ec329ca43a0da6d77e91ef9297d3/scene/3d/physics/joints/joint_3d.cpp#L102\r\n\r\nI've changed the name to `DistanceJoint3D`, added property ranges, and used stiffness instead of frequency","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777277284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777291725","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103958#issuecomment-2777291725","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103958","id":2777291725,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lihvN","user":{"login":"Ewall198","id":8436683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MzY2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8436683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198","html_url":"https://github.com/Ewall198","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T00:41:18Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T00:41:18Z","body":"@Calinou I added property ranges + suffixes.\r\n\r\nThe reason your example doesn't work is because you have the following connections:\r\nBegin <-> Body2\r\nBody1 <-> Body3\r\nBody2 <-> End\r\n\r\nYou want to have the following connections:\r\nBegin <-> Body1\r\nBody1 <-> Body2\r\nBody2 <-> Body3\r\nBody3 <-> End\r\n\r\n[test_pr_103958.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19596505/test_pr_103958.zip)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2d44a147-0d70-4bdd-a1f9-ffd1163c4ee4)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777291725/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2931465693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103958#issuecomment-2931465693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103958","id":2931465693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uup3d","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T16:21:32Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T16:23:38Z","body":"How does this concept map to glTF generic joints? See [OMI_physics_joint](https://github.com/omigroup/gltf-extensions/tree/main/extensions/2.0/OMI_physics_joint) and Microsoft [KHR_physics_rigid_bodies joints](https://github.com/eoineoineoin/glTF_Physics/tree/master/extensions/2.0/Khronos/KHR_physics_rigid_bodies#joints). There is an example of a hanging rope made using pin joints [here](https://github.com/omigroup/omi-godot/blob/main/examples/omi_physics_joint/gltf/hanging_rope.gltf), with rigid bodies acting as the rope.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2931465693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2931559578","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103958#issuecomment-2931559578","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103958","id":2931559578,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uvAya","user":{"login":"Ewall198","id":8436683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MzY2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8436683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198","html_url":"https://github.com/Ewall198","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ewall198/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T16:48:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T17:10:09Z","body":"> How does this concept map to glTF generic joints? See [OMI_physics_joint](https://github.com/omigroup/gltf-extensions/tree/main/extensions/2.0/OMI_physics_joint) and Microsoft [KHR_physics_rigid_bodies joints](https://github.com/eoineoineoin/glTF_Physics/tree/master/extensions/2.0/Khronos/KHR_physics_rigid_bodies#joints). There is an example of a hanging rope made using pin joints [here](https://github.com/omigroup/omi-godot/blob/main/examples/omi_physics_joint/gltf/hanging_rope.gltf), with rigid bodies acting as the rope.\r\n\r\n@aaronfranke This joint constrains min/max distance. Currently there is no other joint which does this in Godot.\r\nUsing a series of pin joints to constrain distance causes a couple different issues:\r\n- When the rope is pulled too hard it may cause the rope to explode and wiggle like crazy as it iterates over the joints and tries to solve them all.\r\n- It doesn't constrain minimum distance.\r\n- It collides with objects, but only in some places. Given enough force, objects will slide through the rope.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2931559578/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940576436","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103958#issuecomment-3940576436","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103958","id":3940576436,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q4Gy0","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T09:29:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T09:29:17Z","body":"Another note: The joint is missing a `get_applied_force` function.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940576436/reactions","total